<title>CANADA: Canadian Air, unions meet on survival plan.</title>
<headline>Canadian Air, unions meet on survival plan.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cash-strapped Canadian Airlines Corp has begun meeting with its unions to discuss a rescue plan for the carrier and believes it is close to concluding a separate contract agreement with its flight attendants, a company spokeswoman said Thursday.</p>
<p>Company executives and officials from its six unions have been holed up in a hotel outside Vancouver all week. But plans to discuss a broad restructuring of the airline including the company's call for a 10 percent wage reduction have been stalled since Tuesday pending efforts to reach a collective agreement with the flight attendants.</p>
</text>
